+\begin{abstract}
+For the lattice $\Lambda=H_1(F,\mathbb Z)$ of a smooth complex two-torus
+fibre in Engel's fibration, we give the two integral monodromy markings
+and determine the primitive invariant alternating form $\xi$, up to sign.  The
+distinguished circle class $\delta_0$ and invariant covector $\psi$ satisfy
+\[
+                 \iota_{\delta_0}\xi=-6\psi.
+\]
+An explicit unimodular basis puts $\xi$ in the form $J\oplus6J$; hence its
+discriminant group is $(\mathbb Z/6\mathbb Z)^2$, with a perfect alternating
+pairing and a six-dimensional irreducible finite Heisenberg representation.
+We also compute the complete Smith form of a two-fibre presentation,
+including the zero-determinant case, and identify its determinant with a
+denominator-cleared Seifert Euler number.  For an explicitly constructed
+effective rank-one Seifert $\mathbb C^*$-bundle with two multiple fibres, we
+prove that the primitive integral Leray carrier is indexed by
+$\operatorname{lcm}(r,s)$ and has coefficient
+$\Delta/\gcd(r,s)$.  The full global Seifert class also has a
+$\mathbb Z/\gcd(r,s)$ component which the coarse transgression does not see.
+We resolve the integral extension hidden by this differential and compute
+the symmetric torsion linking form of every effective two-fibre filling.
+For arbitrary integral local data, the doubled presentation has alternating
+elementary divisors $(d,|\Delta|/d)$, where $d=\gcd(r,s,m,n)$.
+These pairings have specified, distinct carriers.  Engel's rank-four
+transgression remains a separate $(3,4)$ calculation.
+For the same rank-four monodromy, we construct integral chains for gluing
+three torus boundaries with specified filling maps and their homotopies.
+The cusp boundary with transport $T_\infty^h$ has
+$H_2=H_3=\mathbb Z^6\oplus(\mathbb Z/|h|\mathbb Z)^2$ for
+$h\ne0$. Explicit transported cycles determine its prime-coefficient
+connecting homomorphisms. These boundary groups and the complete gluing
+differential specify the further attachments needed for the singular fibres.
+\end{abstract}
